<title>DENMARK: Maersk puts East Africa on container net.</title>
<headline>Maersk puts East Africa on container net.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maersk Line, owned by Denmark's A.P. Moeller shipping and oil group, said on Tuesday it planned from early April to link East African ports to its global container vessel network with new services.</p>
<p>It said that two small 20-ft vessels each with capacity for 400 containers would initially ply the route linking the United Arab Emirates port of Jebel Ali with Dar es Salaam in Tanzania, Mombasa in Kenya and Colombo in Sri Lanka.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
